<description>&lt;p&gt;Algerian troops have moved into Niger to protect energy assets as jihadist attacks increase, while Russian-affiliated forces continue killing civilians in Mali. In Nigeria, police rescued abducted women, farmers and children in multiple states and arrested suspects linked to kidnappings and fake ID operations. Burkina Faso is sending youth to a Russia-Africa summit for training, indicating a shift toward Russian security cooperation. The conflict produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMif0FVX3lxTE9PZEZrRGp3Z2FOWVVsRXZBSWxPY3JodHlyZ1ZSYmhYSnB3TXRPeDRJem02ZFJwbHlCRzBVUHFvUDZ4VFhPMEVjNnBnT3YwS25OZEYxX09adW5lQl9BZklQRzd4c1cxaExlMmJ1ZVRfOThfMldxZWxmR0JPeTJ3a2c?oc=5&quot;&gt;CNN&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXEFVX3lxTE9SWVFtcTBLbmJCbG80RkhHaWdMeXpyZ3ctaUJLekFfWWdoSzY0VGVhS21BM1hhZjhPTE5HQi1pcm42TDZMcFVpMEg5eGxDdndpTTFzWmlQVkx0X1lP?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirgFBVV95cUxPSlJJRTBHcVM0d2RVaUQtaVBkWjRVeGdXZnFPRjVsdzJlUFdreGZnSkZhcWlDYzZYWmNKaWJHQm85Q2t1b1pVQ1N3eUwzMTNEXzMxQ0VQS0c0aUNPdFVQd0hROFZDSEVSSFZQNTBOWWRBTUcxSjI3SmloRGxiaUdWRjVtWWoxYzUyb2h4SXY1dTFybE9RbGREZGhwQllJNHNnUTRPNVBBVzJyTUpqZHc?oc=5&quot;&gt;Daily Beirut&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijgFBVV95cUxPR05JbVFFUWtLaTdxOFZlTEF3SG1SRWF4YTBia3hPVXBTZ3NFWGYzTHFaTXF2UEw0RGtkTUNXX2hPNFRxQmxGOEp0SWlJYVJIX1F4QTFDQ3huSU1nRGZtN2pKbHBrWFRINDh4OXoyTHMxTnhDLVVsamIyOXZGZTBEY3QxWGxyS0hrd3RhazRn?oc=5&quot;&gt;Daily Beirut&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiZEFVX3lxTE1Uc3dNRWJyR0NMVTU2bUtleFJVcERLX2xJYU82UVBQeTR0RDhTVUllTVBvR0tCOTdpMW11QTJOelpVcEllSmoxOXJ1YjVKTU1fa1M5RkZpZ3JzcGk2eFBuWFlRcWs?oc=5&quot;&gt;Daily Trust&lt;/a